WEBVTT

00:05.759 --> 00:11.061
No one can see it.

00:13.200 --> 00:18.939
I close my eyes and think of you,

00:18.939 --> 00:24.969
Who I'll meet someday.

00:25.479 --> 00:31.645
Flower of the wind, please bloom.

00:32.052 --> 00:38.252
Show the spring to these eyes of mine.

00:38.592 --> 00:44.758
Flower of the wind, please bloom.

00:45.065 --> 00:50.970
Farewell to the city in winter.

00:51.605 --> 00:57.874
Flower of the wind, please bloom.

00:58.278 --> 01:04.740
Call the spring to my heart.

01:04.818 --> 01:11.358
Flower of the wind, please bloom.

01:11.358 --> 01:17.729
Farewell, snow flakes.

01:38.652 --> 01:44.324
The Mage Action Request Form
submitted to the nearest office is

01:44.324 --> 01:48.061
initially evaluated for content.
Once the request is officially accepted,

01:48.061 --> 01:51.665
full explanation is given
to the applicant,

01:51.665 --> 01:54.998
and a permit for the requested task is
sent to the mage assigned to the case.

01:55.268 --> 01:59.005
Wow, I only have a month
to learn all this information...

01:59.005 --> 02:02.031
And I still have homework
for the summer break...

02:02.809 --> 02:07.712
"The Best News"

02:09.749 --> 02:11.683
Yume-chan, smile.

02:13.486 --> 02:14.919
Ok, here goes...

02:15.255 --> 02:16.381
Yes!

02:17.123 --> 02:19.125
"Uniform"

02:19.125 --> 02:21.685
Summer
Junior Year
During mage training

02:25.298 --> 02:27.858
Shimo-Kitazawa
Shopping Street

02:28.435 --> 02:32.372
Yume-chan, you go on ahead.
I'm going to buy a newspaper.

02:32.372 --> 02:33.361
Yes.

02:35.175 --> 02:36.676
Good morning, Kuniko-san.

02:36.676 --> 02:40.237
Oh, Oyamada-kun!
Here it is.

02:40.280 --> 02:41.181
"Jumbo Lottery Winning Numbers"

02:41.181 --> 02:43.206
"Jumbo Lottery Winning Numbers"
The Jumbo Lottery winning
numbers from the other day.

02:43.617 --> 02:47.417
Ah, thank you very much.
I'm sorry to bother you.

02:47.587 --> 02:51.216
Oh, you're a regular customer.
It's just part of my job.

02:51.558 --> 02:53.082
See you later.

02:54.427 --> 02:56.224
Wouldn't it be
great if you won?

02:58.064 --> 03:00.624
He looks just like my
husband when he was young...

03:07.607 --> 03:09.598
What? Angela-san?

03:10.310 --> 03:12.946
Master Chief Ginpun's
business trip was extended.

03:12.946 --> 03:16.074
So she'll be training
with us today.

03:20.387 --> 03:22.255
- Ah! It'll stain my skirt!

03:22.255 --> 03:23.347
- Ah! It'll stain my skirt!
- Are you all right?

03:23.657 --> 03:27.821
Yes, I'm all right.
I'm just going to the Ladies Room.

03:33.533 --> 03:34.834
Excuse me.

03:34.834 --> 03:38.031
Do you know where the
Oyamada Mage Labor Office is?

03:39.105 --> 03:42.108
Take this street a little
farther that way.

03:42.108 --> 03:43.710
It's a building with a
bar called "Pachanga"

03:43.710 --> 03:44.938
That woman...

03:45.612 --> 03:48.281
She must be the applicant who's
scheduled to see me today.

03:48.281 --> 03:51.451
Oh, these shoes!
And in all places!

03:51.451 --> 03:53.286
I've been looking
for a pair like this!

03:53.286 --> 03:54.487
I'll take them.

03:54.487 --> 03:55.385
Thank you very much.

03:59.292 --> 04:01.089
- Won't you, please?
- Won't you, please?

04:01.461 --> 04:03.122
Please donate to charity!

04:03.196 --> 04:04.254
Please donate!

04:04.397 --> 04:06.700
Would you like the
shoes in a box?

04:06.700 --> 04:08.335
I'm sorry.
I don't want them anymore.

04:08.335 --> 04:09.336
Uh, excuse me?

04:09.336 --> 04:10.667
Maybe some other time.
I'm sorry.

04:10.904 --> 04:12.098
10,000 yen
(Approx. $85)

04:14.641 --> 04:17.711
What a tough job on a hot day!
Keep up the good work!

04:17.711 --> 04:19.406
- Thank you very much!
- Thank you very much!

04:20.313 --> 04:22.747
I managed to keep it
from staining my skirt.

04:22.916 --> 04:25.783
Yume, our applicant's here.
We'll take a shortcut.

04:25.952 --> 04:26.884
What? Oh, yes.

04:34.694 --> 04:35.922
Excuse me...

04:37.030 --> 04:39.396
Are you looking for
Oyamada-sensei's office?

04:40.066 --> 04:41.090
That's right.

04:41.835 --> 04:45.066
Welcome.
I'll show you in.

04:45.105 --> 04:48.040
General Bureau of Mage Labor,
Tokyo District Certified
Oyamada Mage Labor Office
Certificate #000186

04:51.444 --> 04:52.775
I'm so sorry!

04:54.914 --> 04:56.541
Ah, Angela-san!

04:56.850 --> 04:57.951
An applicant.

04:57.951 --> 05:00.647
Welcome!
I'll open up right now!

05:01.221 --> 05:04.156
You went out knowing that
an applicant was coming?

05:04.357 --> 05:06.120
I'm so sorry, Angela-san.

05:07.527 --> 05:08.687
Just call me Angela.

05:10.063 --> 05:11.155
Please come in.

05:12.399 --> 05:16.130
So, where is the Master
Mage, Oyamada-sensei?

05:16.669 --> 05:17.904
Don't tell me it's you.

05:17.904 --> 05:19.462
Oh, no, not at all!

05:19.639 --> 05:22.540
What the heck are you girls?
Part-timers?

05:22.709 --> 05:24.370
They're trainees.

05:26.379 --> 05:29.716
You must be Goto Ayano-sama.
I'm Oyamada.

05:29.716 --> 05:31.616
First Class, Mage License
Master Mage, Oyamada Masami

05:33.353 --> 05:33.920
Tokyo Prefecture
Mage Labor Request Form

05:33.920 --> 05:35.755
Tokyo Prefecture
Mage Labor Request Form
Now let me verify your request.

05:35.755 --> 05:36.813
Now let me verify your request.

05:37.190 --> 05:38.748
It's exactly what's written there.

05:41.394 --> 05:42.986
Create news out of me.

05:44.297 --> 05:46.197
I want you to make
me a news story.

05:46.699 --> 05:48.860
Indeed, that's what it says here...

05:49.369 --> 05:51.438
But I'm a bit surprised
that such an abstract request

05:51.438 --> 05:53.338
was accepted at the window.

05:54.140 --> 05:56.376
The old guy at the window,
a Mr. Endo or something,

05:56.376 --> 05:59.345
said I could keep it that way, since
I shouldn't lie on my request form.

05:59.679 --> 06:02.341
He said the mage
would handle the rest.

06:02.449 --> 06:04.717
I knew Endo-san had
something to do with it.

06:04.717 --> 06:06.981
Usually a request like
this is not accepted.

06:07.487 --> 06:10.217
I don't want the news
to be about a crime.

06:10.723 --> 06:13.126
If it involves a petty fine
or something, I'll pay.

06:13.126 --> 06:15.720
But I want it to be big.

06:15.795 --> 06:17.831
It'll be even better if I can
have a news conference.

06:17.831 --> 06:21.961
So you're saying that you want
to be on TV or in the newspaper?

06:22.268 --> 06:23.565
Quickly.

06:24.237 --> 06:26.296
Do you mind
telling me the reason?

06:30.844 --> 06:32.779
My reason shouldn't matter.

06:32.779 --> 06:36.112
If you're a mage,
can't you do anything I request?

06:36.349 --> 06:37.150
- Kikuchi-san?

06:37.150 --> 06:38.318
- Kikuchi-san?
- What? Yes...

06:38.318 --> 06:42.489
Please explain to our applicant the
protocol for a Power Action to be taken.

06:42.489 --> 06:43.285
Yes.

06:44.591 --> 06:47.527
Getting as many details as
possible from the applicant

06:47.527 --> 06:50.730
is integral to making
a successful request.

06:50.730 --> 06:53.933
When a mage understands the reasons
for and of the request, he or she will

06:53.933 --> 06:58.461
better relate to the applicant, and accuracy
levels of Special Powers will increase.

06:58.771 --> 07:01.569
That's why, like in
this case, well...

07:01.741 --> 07:02.469
What?

07:02.642 --> 07:05.812
The more abstract the request,
the more details we need so as to use

07:05.812 --> 07:08.474
the most appropriate Special Power.

07:08.848 --> 07:11.918
I see.
So it's not a big deal.

07:11.918 --> 07:14.648
With nothing to lose,
being a mage isn't a bad business.

07:14.954 --> 07:15.688
What?

07:15.688 --> 07:18.491
Even if you don't succeed,
you can just blame it on the client.

07:18.491 --> 07:19.626
- What an easy job!

07:19.626 --> 07:20.888
- What an easy job!
- That's not true!

07:21.995 --> 07:24.797
Mages don't blame anyone!

07:24.797 --> 07:28.067
We're trying to explain to you that we
can do a better job if we have details.

07:28.067 --> 07:30.194
Don't mock Special Power!

07:31.571 --> 07:33.232
Are you from Tohoku?

07:33.640 --> 07:36.336
Yes. I'm from Tono,
in Iwate Prefecture.

07:37.443 --> 07:40.276
What's your opinion
of Special Power?

07:41.314 --> 07:45.045
That they exist for weak people.
That's my opinion.

07:47.921 --> 07:48.751
I've decided.

07:50.056 --> 07:54.959
Oyamada-sensei, I'll have these
two girls use their Special Powers.

07:55.528 --> 07:57.428
Make me news.

08:01.968 --> 08:05.062
She found it easier to talk
to you two than to me.

08:05.605 --> 08:09.302
Therefore, please proceed...
with your Special Power Action.

08:09.709 --> 08:13.270
"One mage action per request."
Don't forget the principle.

08:15.481 --> 08:17.108
Um... Goto-san...

08:17.317 --> 08:18.484
You can call me Ayano.

08:18.484 --> 08:21.419
Then, Ayano-san...
You are, um...

08:21.821 --> 08:23.823
Kikuchi-san,
how old are you now?

08:23.823 --> 08:25.586
Uh... Seventeen.

08:25.892 --> 08:27.360
What about you,
Angela-san?

08:27.360 --> 08:28.759
I'm seventeen.

08:29.195 --> 08:30.890
I was eighteen.

08:31.231 --> 08:32.425
What are you talking about?

08:32.699 --> 08:34.132
When I came to Tokyo.

08:34.567 --> 08:35.468
- From where?

08:35.468 --> 08:36.436
- From where?
- Sendai.

08:36.436 --> 08:37.630
You're kidding!

08:37.770 --> 08:41.501
When I heard your Tohoku dialect,
it reminded me of back home.

08:41.574 --> 08:44.600
When I get excited,
it just comes out.

08:45.011 --> 08:47.605
New Moon
Lila.
I work in Shinjuku at a
hostess bar called "Kyaba-Kura."

08:47.914 --> 08:49.575
Kyaba-Kura?

08:49.749 --> 08:55.187
It's a bar where high-end girls serve
for a cabaret price. Thus, "Kyaba-Kura."

08:55.555 --> 08:57.352
I had no idea
that's what it meant.

08:57.657 --> 09:00.854
There was a guy who
frequented the place to see me.

09:01.160 --> 09:05.096
I'm nice to everyone,
because customers mean money.

09:05.431 --> 09:09.162
But he seriously
proposed to me.

09:09.769 --> 09:14.069
No one ever seriously
told me that I meant so much.

09:17.377 --> 09:20.246
Oh, come on,
don't stare at me like that!

09:20.246 --> 09:23.579
I'm not comfortable talking about it.
Can we walk a little?

09:28.354 --> 09:31.084
There was an embezzlement case
at the company where he worked.

09:31.791 --> 09:34.954
He was in charge of accounting.
But he knew nothing about it.

09:35.828 --> 09:38.729
Yet no excuse was accepted.

09:39.565 --> 09:42.534
Ayano-san, you love him,
too, don't you?

09:42.568 --> 09:43.536
Yes. But he told me
to forget about him.

09:43.536 --> 09:46.539
Recycling Bin for
Bottles and Cans
Yes. But he told me
to forget about him.

09:46.539 --> 09:47.528
Recycling Bin for
Bottles and Cans
Why?

09:51.577 --> 09:54.444
He said I shouldn't date
someone with a criminal record.

09:59.018 --> 10:02.385
Right now he's
serving time in prison.

10:02.922 --> 10:04.657
Have you visited him?

10:04.657 --> 10:07.694
Only his family can visit him.

10:07.694 --> 10:09.787
Also, I don't even know
which prison he's in.

10:10.863 --> 10:14.500
But I found out they're allowed
to read newspapers in prison.

10:14.500 --> 10:16.135
Ah, that's why...

10:16.135 --> 10:19.366
Right. I don't care if I'm on
the first page or the third page.

10:19.739 --> 10:25.078
I just want to become big news
to let him know I'm waiting for him.

10:25.078 --> 10:27.342
So that's why you
wanted to become news.

10:31.651 --> 10:33.243
Huh? What?

10:41.894 --> 10:43.259
Wait a minute!

10:50.670 --> 10:51.771
- What are you doing?

10:51.771 --> 10:52.972
- What are you doing?
- Using my Special Power.

10:52.972 --> 10:54.741
We're supposed to do it together.

10:54.741 --> 10:57.009
Let's discuss what we can do
to make news out of her.

10:57.009 --> 11:00.513
News? Ayano-san just
wants to see him.

11:00.513 --> 11:01.647
So I'll let her see him.

11:01.647 --> 11:04.584
That's not the point. The request
was to make news out of her.

11:04.584 --> 11:06.786
Then use your Special Power
to do that, Yume.

11:06.786 --> 11:07.954
What are you saying?

11:07.954 --> 11:09.888
That her true wish
is just to see him.

11:10.089 --> 11:11.290
That's not her request.

11:11.290 --> 11:13.758
I'll use my Special Power
for the sake of Ayano-san.

11:13.860 --> 11:16.852
Then I, too, will use my Special Power
for the sake of Ayano-san!

11:16.963 --> 11:18.157
Are you sure?

11:18.197 --> 11:19.323
Absolutely!

11:19.565 --> 11:20.657
But can you?

11:20.867 --> 11:22.767
Sure, I can.
I think...

11:27.573 --> 11:30.910
Special Power Level 3 twice.
Level 4 five times.

11:30.910 --> 11:32.969
Verified. Ah, there are more!

11:34.213 --> 11:37.239
Check the ID's of all mages
currently in action! Immediately!

11:38.084 --> 11:44.557
Both mages identified.
They are Class 3, 02441 and 10531.

11:44.557 --> 11:47.890
It's Kikuchi Yume and Angela Brooks!

11:53.966 --> 11:55.668
This isn't exactly
what I had in mind.

11:55.668 --> 11:59.968
Never mind. Enough already.
It's impossible!

12:29.335 --> 12:30.570
What shall I do?

12:30.570 --> 12:33.004
Great Jumbo Lottery Class 34, 107356
The Winning Number Class 34, 1073...

12:33.973 --> 12:35.338
Welcome home!

12:36.309 --> 12:38.010
We're home...

12:38.010 --> 12:39.443
Welcome back, young ladies.

12:39.512 --> 12:42.276
We heard that you two had gone
on a Special Power Action spree.

12:42.748 --> 12:44.010
How did you hear that?

12:44.217 --> 12:46.686
We got a whole bunch of phone calls
from the Bureau of Mage Labor.

12:46.686 --> 12:48.654
Owner's been at his wits' end.

12:49.088 --> 12:50.790
Is he in the bar?

12:50.790 --> 12:53.156
No. He's probably in his office.

12:54.760 --> 12:57.923
Well, don't beat yourself up over it.
You helped someone out, right?

13:01.300 --> 13:02.935
That's the end of my report.

13:02.935 --> 13:06.427
We couldn't use our Special Powers
effectively to make news out of her.

13:06.806 --> 13:08.908
I'm not sure what
we should have done.

13:08.908 --> 13:09.909
- Where's Goto-san?

13:09.909 --> 13:11.177
- Where's Goto-san?
- She went to work.

13:11.177 --> 13:13.611
What does she do for a living?

13:14.146 --> 13:14.914
Kya...

13:14.914 --> 13:16.006
Kyaba-Kura.

13:17.850 --> 13:20.520
Please give us one more chance.

13:20.520 --> 13:23.182
Please. Please let us
try one more time.

13:23.956 --> 13:27.722
The principle is
"One mage action to a request," right?

13:30.363 --> 13:32.999
This case is closed.

13:32.999 --> 13:35.991
Unfortunately it failed,
but things like this happen sometimes.

13:36.502 --> 13:41.440
If you handled this case,
it might have succeeded!

13:41.440 --> 13:43.543
We failed because
I accepted the case

13:43.543 --> 13:49.675
I forgot my place,
and I'm not qualified to be a mage.

13:50.249 --> 13:52.585
Stop thinking that
Special Powers are almighty.

13:52.585 --> 13:53.176
What?

13:53.419 --> 13:56.388
Special Powers are really very limited.

14:00.126 --> 14:03.926
Well, now. Angela, why don't
you spend the night here tonight?

14:04.897 --> 14:07.866
Yume, I'm going out
tonight for a while.

14:08.167 --> 14:10.260
Uh... yes.

14:21.013 --> 14:22.480
Aye-aye, sir.

14:27.453 --> 14:30.149
Angela, you can
take the first shower.

14:31.390 --> 14:34.086
I haven't opened this yet,
so you're welcome to wear them.

14:34.927 --> 14:36.929
You might not like them,
since someone else bought them.

14:36.929 --> 14:39.131
Do you want to go to a
convenience store to buy your own?

14:39.131 --> 14:40.099
- Oh, why?

14:40.099 --> 14:40.967
- Oh, why?
- Huh?

14:40.967 --> 14:43.435
Why did my Special Power fail?

14:43.736 --> 14:46.705
I can't stop thinking about it.

14:49.508 --> 14:51.908
Kabuki-cho 1 st Avenue

15:09.795 --> 15:11.092
Thanks for your help.

15:13.065 --> 15:14.464
That's why...

15:15.835 --> 15:17.637
Good evening!

15:17.637 --> 15:19.238
I'm Lila.

15:19.238 --> 15:21.263
Thank you for requesting me!

15:22.041 --> 15:23.175
Good evening.

15:23.175 --> 15:23.834
Ah!

15:25.411 --> 15:27.003
I've come to have some fun.

15:30.916 --> 15:32.474
I'm sorry it was all leftovers.

15:33.352 --> 15:36.321
Um... Maybe you didn't like it?

15:36.489 --> 15:37.251
No.

15:37.456 --> 15:38.445
I'm glad.

15:40.092 --> 15:40.922
I'm thinking...

15:42.061 --> 15:47.124
Ayano-san's work is
pretty tough, isn't it?

15:47.667 --> 15:51.103
One more time... I want to use
my Special Power on Ayano-san again.

15:51.604 --> 15:52.161
Huh?

15:52.738 --> 15:56.834
I want to use a Special Power that
will convey Ayano-san's feelings to him.

15:57.209 --> 15:59.109
Of course. I do, too.

16:03.582 --> 16:05.607
I'm sorry about today.

16:05.951 --> 16:09.352
Those two girls did
do their best, though.

16:09.689 --> 16:12.089
I won't charge you
the balance of the fee.

16:12.358 --> 16:14.849
You mean the request fee
for Special Powers? Hah!

16:15.394 --> 16:20.127
I'll pay the rest at the
government office... with this!

16:22.034 --> 16:24.670
Great Jumbo Lottery,
but the wrong class.

16:24.670 --> 16:26.638
So I only won a little.

16:28.040 --> 16:32.909
But still, I felt like I might
also try a Special Power action.

16:33.713 --> 16:35.044
Is that so?

16:35.281 --> 16:37.650
I was told at the counter
at the office, too, that the request

16:37.650 --> 16:40.920
was a little too abstract
and it might be difficult...

16:40.920 --> 16:43.122
I'm sorry we couldn't
fulfill your request.

16:43.122 --> 16:48.685
It's all right. I chose those two girls
knowing that they're trainees.

16:48.861 --> 16:50.129
Why was that?

16:50.129 --> 16:51.289
I wonder why, too.

16:51.964 --> 16:57.425
Maybe because their
straightforward passion struck me.

16:58.971 --> 17:01.307
Didn't you hear my
reason for the request?

17:01.307 --> 17:01.966
Yes.

17:02.541 --> 17:06.477
To let a guy in prison know
"I'll be waiting forever."

17:06.545 --> 17:08.911
Am I a fool, or what!

17:26.665 --> 17:29.156
Come in!
We have very lovely ladies...

17:32.972 --> 17:34.607
Sensei, please come again!

17:34.607 --> 17:36.542
Yes. Thank you very much.

17:36.542 --> 17:38.271
Promise me. All right?

17:41.380 --> 17:46.181
Sensei...
I just wanted to be his hope.

17:48.454 --> 17:50.081
You look lonely, too.

17:52.725 --> 17:54.352
Well, thank you very much.

18:02.701 --> 18:05.226
We'll never find the bar.

18:06.972 --> 18:08.633
What'll we do?

18:12.411 --> 18:13.935
Oyamada-sensei!

18:17.249 --> 18:18.910
A salsa club in Shinjuku?

18:19.685 --> 18:23.018
I need to observe other
bars from time to time.

18:23.088 --> 18:24.578
And what about you?

18:25.024 --> 18:26.225
- Um, well, uh...

18:26.225 --> 18:27.214
- Um, well, uh...
- Today...

18:28.494 --> 18:32.521
My Special Power failed.
I couldn't fulfill Ayano-san's request.

18:33.299 --> 18:38.464
So we went looking for her bar to use
Special Power for her one more time.

18:39.605 --> 18:43.598
Angela, you're very smart,
but you still lack something.

18:44.109 --> 18:45.371
What do you mean?

18:49.748 --> 18:52.410
You don't have courage
to acknowledge your failure.

18:54.920 --> 19:00.881
It sounds like you want to
satisfy yourself, instead of Goto-san.

19:03.462 --> 19:07.193
Excuse me. Thank you for
everything. I'm going home tonight.

19:07.466 --> 19:09.263
Ah, Angela!

19:10.436 --> 19:12.996
Oyamada-sensei, we don't
need to stop Angela?

19:16.742 --> 19:18.505
She'll be just fine.

